First let me say that this discussion comes up over and over in this forum.
We have been kicking this around for at least the couple of years that I have
been reading this group.

My personal opinion is that this really should be addressed.  It is endlessly
frustrating to me, to the point that once I have a good digging tool I just
abandon my pets (I know there are other uses for them than robbing shops, but
they don't really do anything worth the frustration of keeping them around).

>What about this one:
>You step into your pet: attack/exchange-position/quit [a/e/q]

I think that you should be allowed to kick your pet without doing damage
or making it mad at you.  The kick is not an attack, it is an attention-
getting device: "Hey, stupid, get out of my way, and keep moving."

Your pet, being a nice, tame, version of his species, will humbly respond most
of the time (unless he is eating or fighting or starving, for example). He
will attempt to move in the direction of your kick, and for the next 4 or 5
turns, at least, he will tend to go the same direction, away from you.

Hey, we are ancient warriors in this game.  Any pet that is too stupid to
respond to an instructive kick in the ribs belongs on a bar-B-Q spit.

